    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a derived, read-only value exposed on the Owner API response. Following the existing pattern for other derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`, `namesakeCount`), which are model getters mapped into the generated `OwnerDto` by MapStruct, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getMembershipTier()` getter returning `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`:\n   ```java\n   public String getMembershipTier() {\n       boolean unique = this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0;\n       boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isEmpty();\n       return unique && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a `membershipTier` string property (readOnly) on the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field and MapStruct maps it by name.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 2/2 tests passing, 0 failures.",
